  "instance_name": "bureaucratic_procedure",
  "label": "Bureaucratic Procedure",
  "description": "The phrase 'state your name for the record' is a standard procedural requirement in formal settings like congressional hearings, legal depositions, or official investigations. The humor arises from the juxtaposition of this serious requirement with the absurd follow-up question 'what page is it on?', implying a person so entrenched in bureaucratic thinking that they forget basic record-keeping. This requires knowledge of how formal proceedings operate and the common expectations around record-keeping.",
